# Findings the "Scan image" step of tests.yml's `image` job accepts. That step already skips vulnerabilities with no
# fix yet (ignore-unfixed), so everything here HAS a fix, just not one we can apply: it ships in an upstream image
# we build FROM, or in a tool inside it. Every entry carries `exp:`: past that date the finding fails CI again, so
# it gets re-checked rather than forgotten. Prefer merging Dependabot's base-image bump (see .github/dependabot.yml)
# and deleting the entry over extending the date.

# caddy:2-alpine, victoria-metrics and victoria-logs: Go standard library built into the upstream binaries. Fixed in
# Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3; waiting on a Caddy / VictoriaMetrics release built with it (Dependabot proposes the tag).
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-24
# The same, fixed in Go 1.26.11 / 1.27.4 (victoria-metrics v1.156.0 is built with 1.27.3).
CVE-2026-97054 exp:2026-11-24

# caddy:2-alpine (brotli-libs) and fluent-bit (libbrotli1): the distro has the fix (Alpine 1.2.1-r0, Debian
# 1.1.0-2+deb13u1) but upstream has not rebuilt the image on it. Neither image decodes untrusted brotli input
# (Caddy's encode directive only compresses responses).
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2026-11-24

# caddy:2-alpine (curl, libcurl): the distro has the fix (Alpine 8.23.0-r0) but upstream has not rebuilt the image
# on it. Nothing in the Caddy container runs curl.
CVE-2026-92392 exp:2026-11-24

# caddy:2-alpine: go-jose/v4 v4.1.5 built into the upstream Caddy binary (DoS parsing JWKs with RSA keys). Fixed in
# 4.1.6; waiting on a Caddy release built with it (Dependabot proposes the tag).
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-11-24

# broker (python:3.14-slim): pip's bundled copies of msgpack, setuptools and urllib3 in the base image's own pip.
# pip is not on the broker's PATH at runtime (the app runs from /app/.venv, which has none) and never runs in the
# container. Goes away with the next python:3.14-slim that ships a newer pip.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-11-24

# broker (python:3.14-slim): msgpack 1.1.2 in the same pip (memory leak deserializing maps), fixed in 1.2.3. Same reasoning
# as above: pip never runs in the container.
CVE-2026-114613 exp:2026-11-24

# caddy and victoria-metrics: golang.org/x/net/html DoS via crafted HTML input (HIGH), fixed in x/net 0.62.0. Vendored in
# the upstream binaries (caddy has v0.59.0, victoria-metrics v0.60.0); waiting on an upstream release that bumps it.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-11-24

# broker (python:3.14-slim) and fluent-bit (debian 13.7): zlib1g 1.3.1-1+b1, fixed in Debian as 1.3.1-1+deb13u1 but not
# yet in the upstream images. The flaws are in zlib's gz* file API (gz_vacate heap overflow) and a webpack-dev-middleware
# title mixed into the zlib entry; neither image reads gzip files through zlib's gz* functions (Python's zlib module and
# Fluent Bit's compression use inflate/deflate streams). Goes away with the next python:3.14-slim / fluent-bit rebuild.
CVE-2026-76844 exp:2026-11-24
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-11-24

# fluent-bit (debian 13.7): libpq5 17.11-0+deb13u1, PostgreSQL's client library, fixed in Debian as 17.12-0+deb13u1 but
# not yet in fluent/fluent-bit:5.2.0. Nearly all are flaws in the PostgreSQL server (code run by SQL functions,
# extensions, reindexdb); Fluent Bit only links the client library for its pgsql output, which fluent-bit.yaml doesn't
# use (it tails logs and sends them over HTTP and remote write), so nothing in the image talks to a PostgreSQL server.
# Goes away with the next fluent-bit rebuild.
CVE-2026-116304 exp:2026-11-29
CVE-2026-116306 exp:2026-11-29
CVE-2026-116307 exp:2026-11-29
